.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-LIST-CERTIFICATES 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-list-certificates \- list the stored certificates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm list-certificates
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the stored certificates with their subject, issuer, fingerprint,
subject alternative names and validity period. Private keys are never
reported.
.PP
Sorting by
.I notAfter
puts the next certificate to expire first, which is what answers what
is about to stop working. A certificate euclid generated for itself is
marked
.IR generated ,
which distinguishes the stopgap the API gateway minted for a listener
from one somebody chose to import.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fITEXT\fR
Only certificates whose name starts with this. Defaults to all.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Page size. Defaults to \fI10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index. Defaults to \fI0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Sort column: \fIname\fR, \fIern\fR or \fInotAfter\fR. Defaults to
\fIname\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The certificates and the total count are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The server could not be reached, or it rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint https://localhost:5566 ekm list-certificates

euclid-cli --endpoint https://localhost:5566 ekm list-certificates \e
    --prefix eag- --sort-column notAfter
.fi
.RE
